{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 14,
  "title": "The body and health",
  "description": "Say what hurts, and how you feel.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Spanish says how you feel with tener followed by a noun: tengo hambre, I am hungry. It is the same pattern as the weather: the verb carries the meaning and the noun says what kind.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How you feel",
        "body": "Tener with a noun says what you are feeling: tengo hambre, tengo sed, tengo sueño, tengo miedo, tengo fiebre. To say you are ill, you use estar: estoy enfermo. To say someone is well, estar sano.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Tengo hambre.",
            "en": "I am hungry."
          },
          {
            "es": "El niño tiene sueño.",
            "en": "The child is sleepy."
          },
          {
            "es": "Estoy enfermo.",
            "en": "I am ill."
          },
          {
            "es": "Mi abuela está sana.",
            "en": "My grandmother is healthy."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where it hurts",
        "body": "A pain is dolor, and it takes the part of the body: me duele la cabeza, me duele el estómago. The verb doler works oddly: it is the body part that is the subject, and the person who feels it uses me, te, le.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "Me duele la cabeza.",
            "en": "I have a headache."
          },
          {
            "es": "Le duele el estómago.",
            "en": "He has a stomach ache."
          },
          {
            "es": "¿Te duele la pierna?",
            "en": "Does your leg hurt?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "Saying you are unwell",
        "body": "A short phrase for a doctor is estar indispuesto, and estar malo means to be unwell or to taste bad. The word for a clinic is la clínica.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "No he ido al trabajo porque estoy indispuesto.",
            "en": "I have not gone to work because I am unwell."
          },
          {
            "es": "Necesitas ir a la clínica.",
            "en": "You need to go to the clinic."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
